Issues Fixed

1. Inference Chat Request Tracking

The inference chat system lacked proper debugging capabilities, making it difficult to troubleshoot when requests weren't reaching the server. Added comprehensive console logging markers throughout the request flow:

// Client-side logging in useNonCustodialChat hook
console.log('[CHAT] start - Beginning non-custodial chat request')
console.log('[CHAT] prepared - Preparing compute request...')
console.log('[CHAT] fetch - Sending to chat API...', { endpoint, hasHeaders })

// Server-side logging in API routes
console.log('[CHAT] HIT - Using non-custodial mode - proxying prepared request')
console.log('[PROXY] HIT - POST https://provider.0g.ai/chat/completions')
This enables developers to trace the complete request path from client → chat API → proxy → 0G provider.

2. Metadata Sync Interference in Development

Background metadata synchronization was causing ENOENT errors and slowing down the development server. Implemented proper environment-based control:

// Server-side check in /api/sync/metadata
const isIndexingEnabled = process.env.INDEXING_WATCHER_ENABLED !== 'false'
if (!isIndexingEnabled) {
  return NextResponse.json({
    success: true,
    message: 'Metadata sync is disabled',
    disabled: true
  })
}

// Client-side hook respect for environment
const isIndexingEnabled = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_INDEXING_WATCHER_ENABLED !== 'false'
const shouldSync = enabled && isIndexingEnabled
Now developers can set INDEXING_WATCHER_ENABLED=false to disable background sync during development.

3. Environment Configuration Verification

Enhanced environment loading verification and proper separation of server-side vs client-side configuration:

# Server-side only (private keys)
INDEXING_WATCHER_ENABLED=false
OG_STORAGE_PRIVATE_KEY=0x...

# Client-side accessible
NEXT_PUBLIC_INDEXING_WATCHER_ENABLED=false
NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_NONCUSTODIAL_INFERENCE=true
The dev server now properly shows "Environments: .env.local" confirming configuration is loaded.

4. Enhanced Error Handling for Missing Files

Improved the /api/storage/retrieve route to handle missing metadata files gracefully:

} catch (fileError) {
  console.log('[Storage Retrieve] Local file not found:', cleanRootHash)
  // Continue to fallback instead of throwing ENOENT
}
